.TH AVR\-BUILDER\-LIST 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-builder-list \- List builder sessions, newest first.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr builder list
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List builder sessions, newest first.
.PP
Sessions are never hard-deleted, so terminal (STOPPED/FAILED) sessions keep appearing here; filter with --state RUNNING to see only live ones. Non-admin members see only their own sessions.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr builder list
    avr builder list --state RUNNING
    avr builder list --json builder_session_id,state,stop_at
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    builder_session_id, cpu_count, created_at, disk_gb, memory_mb, platform,
    repository_full_name, state, state_reason, stop_at, updated_at
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Filter by state. (choices: PENDING, STARTING, RUNNING, STOPPING, STOPPED, FAILED)
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Max sessions. (default: 50)
.TP
\fB\-\-cursor\fR \fITEXT\fR
Pagination cursor from a previous response.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-builder (1),
.BR avr-builder-stop (1)
